+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, a key from `apiKeys` in
+the data. Without a key, or with one that is not known, the answer is 401
+`unauthorized` (also for routes that do not exist). A known key whose role
+does not allow the request gets 403 `forbidden`.
+
+- `viewer`: every `GET` except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: the same, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures` and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: everything, including `GET /audit`.
+
+A route that is not a `GET` needs `manager` unless it names a lower role
+(the fourth element of the route in `src/http/routes/`).
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that is not a `GET` and carries a known key writes one audit
+entry, whether it succeeded or not (a refused or failed attempt is recorded
+with its status). Requests answered 401 are not recorded: there is no key to
+name.
+
+    { "id": 3, "at": "2026-10-28T10:00:00.000Z", "keyName": "line cook",
+      "method": "POST", "path": "/recipes/1/cook", "status": 200 }
+
+`path` is without the query string. `GET /audit` lists the entries newest
+first and is for managers only.
+
